                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "66087840",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198019816374",
                            "num_reviews": 1791,
                            "playtime_forever": 6,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 6,
                            "last_played": 1585488003
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "There is absolutely no explanation for any of the game's mechanics.\nEvery characters has like 10 abilities and no context around any of it.\nI haven't been this frustrated by a game in a long time.\nAvoid this until it gets a huge update that includes a tutorial.\n(My playtime didn't register properly. I actually played for about 20 minutes.)\n\nhttps://youtu.be/qI24NuSM3dI",
                        "timestamp_created": 1585488052,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1585488052,
                        "voted_up": false,
                        "votes_up": 67,
                        "votes_funny": 5,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.7545086741447449,
                        "comment_count": 10,
                        "steam_purchase": false,
                        "received_for_free": true,
                        "written_during_early_access": true,
                        "developer_response": "You go into a hardcore tactical game. That's what our press letter has said.\nYou pay no mind to the mission. You don't read its description, you don't bother to check if the missions do differ.\nYou send just whomever to the mission. You don't read their equipment, you don't care what they do.\nIn mission you also don't read around, you just do random stuff without paying much attention. Through all the video, you mostly ignore all the information that the game throws at you.\n\nQuestion - if there was a tutorial, would you bother to read it? From our previous experience (we've invested quite a lot into our previous game's tutorial - scripted chapters, pop-up messages, video previews) - no, you would've just skipped all those tutorials as well.\n\nYou're just a casual player who wants to PWN from the get-go. There's nothing wrong to it but, perhaps, you should be also paying attention to press releases and keep in mind that \"hardcore\" sometimes means \"hardcore\" and is not an empty press talk.",
                        "timestamp_dev_responded": 1585493999,
